Bendy is not the same as broken. If your nails feel like they could fold in half the moment you removed your gel or acrylics, that is not permanent damage, it is a temporary state your nail plate moves through on its way back to normal. <strong>How to repair nails after gel acrylic removal</strong> comes down to two things: knowing the real timeline, and following a routine that rebuilds strength instead of just masking the problem. Most people expect their nails to bounce back within days. They do not. What we can tell you, precisely, is how long it actually takes and what to do starting today. This guide covers exactly that: why the thinness happens, the week-by-week recovery, the daily routine, and the red flags that mean it is time to see a professional.

